Chapter: DtlsAuthLoopbackTest
  cites Net chapter DtlsEndpoint
  cites Encode chapter X509
  cites Encode chapter X509Chain
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 An AUTHENTICATED DTLS 1.3 handshake, end to end, over datagrams, with no
 network -- and the negative that proves it is authentication and not
 decoration.

 The server presents a real Ed25519 leaf certificate and signs the
 transcript with its private key. The certificate chain was minted outside
 Codex: the DER was built by .NET's ASN.1 writer and the signatures by our
 own RFC-8032-gated Ed25519 (the forge in scratchpad/forge). The client
 carries the CA as its trust anchor.

 UNLIKE THE ANONYMOUS LOOPBACK, THIS ONE AUTHENTICATES. If test-mitm below
 is not "not-done", the man-in-the-middle defence is broken and nothing
 here is secure.

